# Aeration Blower Delayed Start - ST Implementation

## Analysis

The solution requires:
1. A delay timer that starts when both `DO_LOW` AND `AERATION_E_STOP_NC` are TRUE
2. Timer must reset immediately when either condition becomes FALSE
3. Rising edge detection on `BLOWER_RUN` for cycle counting
4. Proper initialization on power-up

## Implementation

```st
PROGRAM AerationBlowerControl
VAR
    // Inputs
    DO_LOW                : BOOL;
    AERATION_E_STOP_NC    : BOOL;

    // Outputs
    BLOWER_RUN                    : BOOL;
    AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT   : UINT := 0;

    // Internal variables
    StartTimer        : TON;
    BlowerRunPrev     : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Start Delay Logic
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Conditions for starting: DO is low AND emergency stop is inactive
IF DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC THEN
    // Start the 5-second delay timer
    StartTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := T#5S);

    // Enable blower only after timer completes
    IF StartTimer.Q THEN
        BLOWER_RUN := TRUE;
    ELSE
        BLOWER_RUN := FALSE;
    END_IF;
ELSE
    // Conditions not met - immediately disable blower
    BLOWER_RUN := FALSE;

    // Reset the start timer (timer IN = FALSE)
    StartTimer(IN := FALSE);
END_IF;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Start Cycle Counting
// Detect FALSE-to-TRUE transition of BLOWER_RUN
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IF BLOWER_RUN AND NOT BlowerRunPrev THEN
    AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT := AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT + 1;
END_IF;

// Store previous state for edge detection
BlowerRunPrev := BLOWER_RUN;

END_PROGRAM
```

## Explanation

| Component | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| **Timer Start** | `StartTimer(IN:=TRUE)` begins when `DO_LOW=TRUE` AND `AERATION_E_STOP_NC=TRUE` |
| **Timer Reset** | `StartTimer(IN:=FALSE)` immediately resets accumulated time when conditions drop |
| **Blower Enable** | `BLOWER_RUN` sets TRUE only after `StartTimer.Q` becomes TRUE (5 seconds elapsed) |
| **Blower Disable** | `BLOWER_RUN` FALSE whenever start conditions are unmet (emergency stop or low DO) |
| **Cycle Count** | Increments on rising edge: `BLOWER_RUN=TRUE` AND `BlowerRunPrev=FALSE` |
| **Initialization** | `:=0` and `:=FALSE` initial values ensure power-up state is OFF/zero |

The `TON` timer retains its accumulated time when `IN` goes FALSE, but since the requirement specifies "wait the full 5 seconds again" after any interruption, resetting the timer via `IN:=FALSE` is correct behavior.

